# Modal, toast and keyboard

A modal dialog (Escape closes it, focus moves to it on open and back to the
opener on close) and a toast (shown, dismissed by hand).

## Note

The backdrop and the modal card are SIBLINGS, not a parent/child pair, each
positioned with CSS. `on-click.stop` would be the more obvious way to keep a
click inside the card from also closing it via the backdrop's own handler,
but `.stop` refuses to build for the browser at all
(`work/lgx-ease/gauntlet.md` finding G9) — siblings need no event modifier
this tier cannot lower, since a click inside the card never reaches an
ancestor it does not have.

The close button focuses itself from `After 100ms:` rather than
`When this component appears:` — the latter runs before the component's own
markup reaches the DOM, so it cannot focus its own element yet (finding
G13). 100ms is imperceptible and still a real, later turn.

## Component Modal (close: fn() -> Unit)

Actions:
    After 100ms:
        Focus "#close-modal".

    To noop:
        Return.

View:
    <div id="backdrop" class="backdrop" on-click={close}></div>
    <div id="modal" class="modal">
      <h2 id="modal-title" on-click={noop}>Delete this item?</h2>
      <p>This cannot be undone.</p>
      <button id="close-modal" on-click={close}>Cancel</button>
    </div>

## Page /

State:
    Let modalOpen be false.
    Let toastMessage be "".
    Let toastVisible be false.

Actions:
    To openModal:
        Set modalOpen to true.

    To closeModal:
        Set modalOpen to false.
        Focus "#open-modal".

    When the user presses Escape:
        Set modalOpen to false.

    To showToast:
        Set toastMessage to "Saved.".
        Set toastVisible to true.

    To dismissToast:
        Set toastVisible to false.

View:
    <main class="page">
      <h1>Modal, toast and keyboard</h1>
      <button id="open-modal" on-click={openModal}>Open modal</button>
      {if modalOpen:}<Modal close={closeModal}/>{end}
      <button id="show-toast" on-click={showToast}>Show toast</button>
      {if toastVisible:}
        <div id="toast" class="toast">
          <span id="toast-message">{toastMessage}</span>
          <button id="dismiss-toast" on-click={dismissToast}>&times;</button>
        </div>
      {end}
    </main>

Style:
    .backdrop { position: fixed; inset: 0; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, .4); }
    .modal { position: fixed; top: 30%; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); background: var(--paper); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.5rem; }
    .toast { position: fixed; bottom: 1rem; right: 1rem; background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: .5rem 1rem; }

## Test: the modal starts closed

Expect that "#modal" is hidden.

## Test: opening the modal shows it and moves focus inside it after it mounts

Click "#open-modal".
Expect that "#modal" is visible.
Advance time by 200ms.
Expect that "#close-modal" is focused.

## Test: clicking the backdrop closes the modal

Click "#open-modal".
Click "#backdrop".
Expect that "#modal" is hidden.

## Test: clicking inside the modal does not close it, because it is not inside the backdrop

Click "#open-modal".
Click "#modal-title".
Expect that "#modal" is visible.

## Test: the close button closes the modal and returns focus to the opener

Click "#open-modal".
Click "#close-modal".
Expect that "#modal" is hidden.
Expect that "#open-modal" is focused.

## Test: Escape closes the modal from the keyboard

Click "#open-modal".
Press "Escape".
Expect that "#modal" is hidden.

## Test: the toast shows and dismisses by hand

Expect that "#toast" is hidden.
Click "#show-toast".
Expect that the text of "#toast-message" is equal to "Saved.".
Click "#dismiss-toast".
Expect that "#toast" is hidden.
